    {
      "id": "happiness",
      "name": "Happiness",
      "route": "Activate Festivals",
      "url": "https://universalmind.tv/events/happiness-entry.php",
      "source": "https://universalmind.tv/happiness/#about-panel",
      "source_file": "happiness/index.php",
      "access": "The festival experience uses the existing invitation login. These About excerpts are public.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Happiness is a universal happiness currency for festivals globally, powered via Apple Watch. Attendees at festivals are rewarded when they are safe, healthy and happy, together as one.",
        "Happiness also powers a real time public health & safety index for festivals, mitigating risk. People own their data and ethics are via The Ethics Centre and Center for Humane Technology, in conjunction with Apple Watch, together as one.",
        "Our mission is lowering the mass cancelation of festivals globally, via lowering the cost of risk mitigation for festivals, including user pays police, security, medical and insurance, while ensuring events are safe and healthy, together as one."
      ],
      "context": [
        "The About text describes the project and its mission. Named technologies and organisations are not, by their inclusion here, confirmation of a formal partnership or independently validated clinical performance."
      ],
      "source_sha256": "6fd634e6f4fbff09dc0c34b41721ee749313a45be60d79ca8cb5e2037534ca67"
    },
    {
      "id": "informatics",
      "name": "Universal Informatics",
      "route": "Explore Research",
      "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/",
      "source": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/?about",
      "source_file": "Informatics/index.html",
      "access": "The research wiki, publication records and download directory are public. API and MCP access are optional.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Bioinformatics platform for mental health. Investigating potential relationships between the Fibonacci sequence and OXTR gene expression."
      ],
      "about_blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Does modular compression reveal statistically significant patterns, or merely mathematical elegance?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Do the nested sequences within Fibonacci Pisano periods have biological and molecular implications?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Initial focus · Computer vision for genomics"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Inspired by research into how geometric architectures and Fibonacci-ordered dynamics can protect quantum information, we are investigating whether geometry derived from Fibonacci Pisano periods can improve the computational efficiency of hyperspectral image analysis for genomics."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "A measurable first step"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Our proposed approach explores equilateral triangular meshes and tetrahedral models, comparing computational cost, processing speed and accuracy against established methods."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The initial biological application is to investigate spectral patterns potentially associated with OXTR gene expression, evaluated against independent molecular measurements."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Learn the mathematics"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "What is modular arithmetic?",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modular_arithmetic"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Modular arithmetic and spatial mapping in biology"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Decoding spatial position through grid cells",
          "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4730856/"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Science Advances · 2015"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Toroidal geometry in neural activity",
          "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-04268-7"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Nature · 2022"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Science and Open Questions",
          "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/genomics.html"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Future expansion · an OXTR-centred network"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "If independent studies verify biological significance in the OXTR–Fibonacci relationship, we plan to extend the investigation to a wider set of candidate genes and molecular systems."
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Phase Zulu · Explore the candidate network ↗",
          "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/?about"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Sound Research ↗",
          "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/library.html?collection=sound"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Vision Research ↗",
          "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/library.html?collection=vision"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Language Research ↗",
          "url": "https://universalmind.tv/informatics/library.html?collection=language"
        },
        {
          "kind": "link",
          "text": "Symbolic computation with Wolfram",
          "url": "https://www.wolfram.com/"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Wolfram is our planned primary computational environment for symbolic geometry and future bioinformatic research."
        }
      ],
